      <div type="clause" n="34.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ECfRetr">ECf retr</ref> 34.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="ECf retr 34.3"><pb n="663" ed="#liebermann"/>Sed postquam rex Eadwardus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.3"/> uenit ad regnum, consilio baronum <hi rend="bold">Anglie</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.31"/> legem LXVIII<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.27"/> <hi rend="spaced">annis</hi> <hi rend="bold">sopitam excitauit, excitatam</hi> <hi rend="spaced">reparauit</hi>, <hi rend="bold">reparatam decorauit</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.32"/><hi rend="bold">, decoratam</hi> <hi rend="spaced">confirmauit</hi>; <hi rend="bold">confirmata uero</hi> uocata<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.23"/> est lex Eadwardi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.33"/> regis, <hi rend="bold">non</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="i" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.fn.i"/> <hi rend="bold">quod</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.34"/> <hi rend="bold">ipse primus</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.35"/> <hi rend="bold">adinuenisset</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.36"/> <hi rend="bold">eam, sed, cum pretermissa fuisset et</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.37"/> <hi rend="bold">obliuioni penitus tradita</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.38"/> <hi rend="bold">a diebus</hi> aui sui <hi rend="bold">regis</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.30"/> Eadgari<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.star2"/><hi rend="bold">, qui primus</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="39" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.39"/> <hi rend="bold">inuentor eius fuisse dicitur,</hi> usque ad sua tempora, <hi rend="bold">uidelicet</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="40" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.40"/> <hi rend="bold">ut predictum est,</hi> LXVIII annis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="41" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.41"/> <hi rend="bold">post dies</hi> <pb n="664" ed="#liebermann"/><hi rend="bold">ipsius</hi> Eadgari†, <hi rend="bold">ipse</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.1-p664"/> Eadwardus, quia <hi rend="bold">iusta erat</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.2-p664"/> et honesta, <hi rend="bold">a</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.3-p664"/> <hi rend="bold">profunda</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.4-p664"/> <hi rend="bold">abysso extraxit</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.5-p664"/> <hi rend="bold">eam</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.6-p664"/> <hi rend="bold">et renouauit et</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.1-p664"/> <hi rend="bold">ut suam obseruandam</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.7-p664"/> <hi rend="bold">contradidit</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ECfRetr_34-3.lnote.la.8-p664"/><hi rend="bold">.</hi></ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="663"><label>printed alongside</label> <ref target="clause:ECf_34-3">ECf 34.3</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 663–664 (November 2026): read from the page images and checked against the scan’s own text layer, differences settled against the page; the words in bold are the Retractator’s changes to ECf, as Liebermann prints them.</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann’s numbering of the notes in the ECf retr column starts again at 1 on p. 664: the notes 1–8 to the part of this clause on p. 664 are distinct from the notes on p. 663.</note>
        <note type="editorial">Beside the beginning of this clause Liebermann gives the date 1042 in the margin; beside the starred note (**, printed across p. 663) the dates †959–75; and beside “Eadgari†” on p. 664 the date †975.</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann’s note 30 (“fehlt Hr”) names a manuscript of ECf, not of the Retractator; it may be a misprint for Hv.</note>
        <note type="editorial">The note on the London collection’s addition (**) is printed across the whole of p. 663; it is given with both columns.</note>
