        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude-crib" ana="#fromLatin">But after King Edward came to the kingdom, by the counsel of the barons of England he awakened the law that had slept for sixty-eight years, restored it once awakened, adorned it once restored, confirmed it once adorned; and once confirmed it was called the law of King Edward, not because he himself had first devised it, but because, when it had been passed over and entirely consigned to oblivion from the days of his grandfather King Edgar, who is said to have been its first inventor, until his own time, namely, as has been said before, for sixty-eight years after the days of this Edgar†, this Edward, because it was just and honourable, drew it out of the deep abyss and renewed it and handed it over to be observed as his own.</ab>
